  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "**N****val[i]****i****X****Y****a, b**\n\n**a** belongs to **X**, **b** belongs to **X** and **val[a]*val[b]%N = 1**\n**a** belongs to **Y**, **b** belongs to **Y** and **val[a]*val[b]%N = 1**\n**a** belongs to **X**, **b** belongs to **X**, **a** is an ancestor of **b** and **gcd(val[a],val[b]) &gt; 1**\n\nReport if it is possible to select such a subset of nodes.",
    "constraints": [
      "1 <= T <= 200000",
      "1 <= N <= 200000",
      "Sum of all N over all test cases <= 200000",
      "1 <= val[i] < N",
      "1 <= x, y <= N",
      "x != y"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "The first line contains an integer T, the number of test cases. Each test case starts with an integer N, the number of nodes. The next line contains N space-separated integers, the values of the nodes. The following N-1 lines contain two space-separated integers, the edges of the tree.",
    "outputFormat": "For each test case, output 'Yes' if it is possible to select a subset of nodes that satisfy the conditions, and 'No' otherwise.",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "1\n3\n1 2 3\n1 2\n2 3\n1 3",
        "output": "Yes",
        "explanation": "We can select the subset {1, 3} which satisfies the conditions."
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_2",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "1\n4\n1 2 3 4\n1 2\n2 3\n3 4\n1 4",
        "output": "No",
        "explanation": "There is no subset that satisfies the conditions."
      }
    ]
  },
