  "solution": {
    "approach": "To solve this problem, we can use a graph theory approach. We can create a graph where each node represents a value, and two nodes are connected if their product is congruent to 1 modulo N. We can then use a depth-first search (DFS) to find a subset of nodes that satisfy the conditions. We also need to check if there are any nodes that are ancestors of other nodes and have a greatest common divisor (GCD) greater than 1.",
    "timeComplexity": "O(T * (N + M)) — where T is the number of test cases, N is the number of nodes, and M is the number of edges. The DFS takes O(N + M) time, and we need to do this for each test case.",
